# ThreadSanitizer suppressions for the crash-sweep runs (docs/ios-port/SANITIZERS.md). Format: <kind>:<function or module pattern>.
# Added only after the report was read and judged to be noise; every entry says why.

# LuaJIT's assembly interpreter (lj_vm.S) and the JIT'ed machine code are not instrumented, and the VM is single-threaded by
# contract (one lua_State at a time, the engine takes the script lock); what TSan sees of it is the C half racing with itself
# across the engine's coroutine hand-offs.

# ---- by design: the secondary thread (mt_Thread: seqParallel, seqFrameMT) runs while the primary thread renders ----
# The engine hands work between the two threads with the mt_csEnter / mt_csLeave pair and with per-frame counters, not with locks
# around the data. What TSan sees are scalars, flags and per-frame buffers that one side writes and the other reads one frame
# later or earlier; a stale value costs a frame of wrong occlusion, a fade, a physics flag. None of them is a container or a lifetime.

# the engine's one global CRandom, advanced by every thread (render, HOM, physics, particles): a lost update repeats a number
race:CRandom::randI
# hierarchical occlusion map: rebuilt by the secondary thread (CHOM::MT_RENDER), tested by the render phase
race:CHOM::*
race:xform_b0
# Device.dwFrame and g_bRendering: written by the primary thread in Begin()/End(), read by the secondary thread and the prefetcher
race:CRenderDevice::Begin
race:CRenderDevice::End
race:CRenderDevice::on_idle
race:mt_Thread
race:CLevelSoundManager::Update
race:CALifeUpdateManager::update_switch
race:CModelPool::Delete
# the physics step writes element flags that the bones callback of the render phase reads
race:CPHElement::PhDataUpdate
race:CPHElement::BonesCallBack
# crows: flags set while rendering (MakeMeCrow), read by the network processor of the secondary thread
race:CObject::MakeMeCrow
race:CObjectList::net_Export
race:CAI_Crow::net_Export
race:CHUDState::*
# spatial database: sector pointers of the objects, written by the render phase, read by the secondary thread's queries
race:ISpatial::spatial_updatesector_internal
race:ISpatial::spatial_move
# the grass (detail manager): the secondary thread computes next frame's visible slots (MT_CALC) behind the m_frame_rendered /
# m_frame_calc counters while the render phase dumps this frame's; the counters are volatile, not acquire/release. OPEN ITEM
# (SANITIZERS.md): the hand-off is not proven, a late dump of the shadow pass can overlap it
race:CDetailManager::*
# shader compile on the spawn prefetcher's thread reads render options that the render phase changes per frame (RImplementation.o)
race:CBlender_Compile::_cpp_Compile
# static shared_str s_bones_array_const, assigned by the first model load on whichever thread gets there first
race:CSkeletonX::_Load
